From 3b684fac85a43f509bbec6d66c671941788b3d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] drm/panfrost: Refuse to sync the CPU caches of a heap
 BO

On a coherent GPU, PANFROST_SYNC_BO on a heap BO builds an sg table
from the fault handler's sparse page array and dereferences its NULL
entries. Heap BOs cannot be CPU-mapped, so there is nothing to sync:
return -EINVAL, as for imported BOs. Not tested on a coherent GPU.

Fixes: 7be45f548976 ("drm/panfrost: Add a PANFROST_SYNC_BO ioctl")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/sashiko-outbox-206561@kernel.org/
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c
index 3a7fce4..cf2dd45 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c
@@ -557,6 +557,14 @@ panfrost_gem_sync(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type, u32 offset, u32 size)
 	if (drm_gem_is_imported(&shmem->base))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* Heap BOs are not CPU-mappable, and their pages are populated by the
+	 * GPU fault handler, one 2 MB chunk at a time, with a page array and
+	 * sg tables of its own: drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt() must not touch
+	 * them.
+	 */
+	if (bo->is_heap)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	switch (type) {
 	case PANFROST_BO_SYNC_CPU_CACHE_FLUSH:
 	case PANFROST_BO_SYNC_CPU_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INVALIDATE:
-- 
